From: lzwei196 <lzweijinwei196@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:37:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] KI file tools: list one folder at a time, find files by
 name, name the real ones on a miss

list_ki_files lists ONE folder (SKILL.md and dag.yaml first, sub-folders with
file counts; hidden, cache and backup entries counted, not listed) and takes a
`pattern` to find files by name (plain words, or a glob; * and ? stay in one
name, ** crosses folders; case ignored). A missing folder answers with the real
folders nearby; read_ki_file on a missing name answers "Did you mean ...".

Brought over from the GeoForge web agent (live there since 2026-11-05): a small
model (Qwen 27B) looped on the old tools, asking 123 times for a folder that did
not exist (the old answer was "(empty)") and guessing 21 file names.

Kept from the desktop: the intake KI list, paged reading (_read_text_page) and
KI scoping. Walks skip unreadable folders and never follow links or Windows
junctions. Tool names are unchanged, so the flow gate needs no change.

Tests: new test_ki_file_tools.py (6); test_flowgate and test_ki_intake now
check the one-folder listing, a subdir and a pattern. Full suite on Linux:
same 244 failures and 329 errors as windows-version cf3b765a, 6 more passes.
