- Globs: a run of wildcards counts as one (***** = **); ** may appear once, plus once at the
  very end (**/*.py, docs/**, .kdt_runs/** still work); DOTALL so ** covers a newline in a
  name as * does. At most one ** can backtrack, so a match costs about (path length)^2 steps.
  Same answers as the plain translation on 30,000+ generated cases (names with newlines too).
- A fixed folder that two folders match (Data/ and data/) walks from the base instead.
- Hints: values written as JSON strings (quotes and backslashes survive); a KI name is kept
  exactly as given (" B "); in intake a name-search hint names the KI's folder
  (list_ki_files(subdir="Demo", pattern=...)); "./Demo/..." keeps the Demo/ prefix.
- A search cut off at the file limit says so in its first line; counting also charges each
  folder visited; an entry that cannot be read is listed as "(cannot read)".
- Tests: worst-case globs under a hard SIGALRM stop, case-only folder names, quoted hints read
  back exactly, intake hints followed through execute_tool.
