Subject: [PATCH 04/11] KI file tools: review r3 fixes (hard limit on matching,
 intake paths as patterns, case rule)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Matching has a hard limit: KI paths longer than 512 characters are not matched (counted once
  and named in the answer), and one search stops matching after 3 s and says so. Review r3 found
  an allowed pattern that takes ~0.1 s per 3,000-character path; no pattern rule bounds that,
  this does.
- The start-folder shortcut compares names with the pattern's own case rule (re.IGNORECASE),
  so Σ/σ/ς and Data/data fall back to a full walk the same way.
- Intake: a path copied from a listing (Demo/...) works as a pattern; placeholder hints keep
  Demo/; "Demo" as a file path suggests subdir="Demo" (not "Demo/."); a whitespace-only KI name
  is kept in hints as accepted.
- An unreadable hidden entry is not shown as a folder; the ** message names '**/tests/**'.
- Tests: the intake hint is followed exactly as written (parsed from the message); long-path and
  time limits; cut-off first line; junctions in counting and as a start folder; unreadable
  entries; Unicode case.
