From: lzwei196 <lzweijinwei196@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:22:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] KI file tools: review r4 fixes (one time budget per
 call, intake path patterns keep their meaning)

- One 5 s budget covers a whole list/find/miss call: both walks, matching, the hidden retry
  and the hints. Folders count toward the walk cap (50,000 files and folders), so empty folders
  cannot run on. "Close spelling" (difflib) scores at most 2,000 distinct names and is skipped
  when the budget is spent. A slow second walk keeps its hits.
- The 512-character limit applies to path patterns only; a name search reads only the name.
- When anything was skipped, the first line says "in the part of the KI that was searched".
- Intake: a pattern copied from a listing keeps its meaning after Demo/ is taken off
  ("Demo/*.py" = the top folder only, "Demo/" = everything, "./Demo/..." and any case work);
  the empty-folder placeholder keeps Demo/.
- Tests: whole-call budget with 10,000 similar long names, slow hidden walk, 512/513 boundary
  and a timed worst shape, intake prefix meaning (also through execute_tool), a test line that
  could not fail.
