From: lzwei196 <lzweijinwei196@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:31:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] KI file tools: review r5 fixes (one deadline per tool
 call through every step; walked paths always matched)

- One deadline is made when the tool call starts and passed to every step: listing and counting,
  the start-folder shortcut, both walks, matching, the hidden retry, close-name and folder hints,
  and the missing-folder ancestors. All steps read the clock through _ki_now (tests replace it).
- A walk stopped by the budget keeps every folder it read, and matching always gets at least 1 s
  for paths already walked, so a slow disk gives partial answers instead of none.
- "Close spelling" is scored like difflib.get_close_matches but looks at the clock every 100 names;
  folder hints stop at 8 names; a wide folder cannot push the walk past its cap.
- Intake: "././Demo/...", "Demo//", "Demo/." work; a bare "Demo" stays a name search; a hidden
  answer says when only part of the KI was searched.
- Tests: fake clocks for a walk and a hidden retry cut by time, every step against a passed
  deadline, 50,000 folder names, a wide folder, the ~199-character close-spelling worst case,
  intake prefix forms, and flow hints with KI names 'B "q"' and ' C ' followed as written.
