From deb7c8a288c5babfc70f9374b520f33d801a712f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lzwei196 <lzweijinwei196@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:49:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] KI file tools: review r7 fixes (no late look in
 counting or os.walk; no late first read)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Counting checks the clock before each sub-folder's link check.
- Both walks pass followlinks=True: links and junctions are already taken out of dirs by our own
  lstat + reparse-tag check (which also catches junctions that islink misses), so os.walk makes
  no islink look of its own (Python 3.12+ made one per folder, with no clock check).
- No first read after the budget: a listing whose time is spent says "not read" instead of
  scanning; the missing-folder ancestor loop and scan, and the missing-file checks and scan, look
  at the clock first.
- Entries not checked in time are still sorted by name: hidden and backup names go to the hidden
  count, SKILL.md / dag.yaml stay first. "1 entry was" / "N entries were".
- A missing-file answer says it was partial even when it has a suggestion.
- The subdir prefix is cut where the case-insensitive match really ends (İ).
- Unused imports left by the execute_tool split removed.
- Tests: counting looks after the deadline (zero), unchecked names sorted, the call deadline set
  before the roots and reset after (only for the two KI file tools), the partial note with a
  suggestion, and a flow KI named " " followed as written.
