MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Back to followlinks=False in both walks (codex r8: on Python 3.12+ os.walk checks islink just
  before entering a folder, a narrower window than our earlier check alone). Our lstat + reparse
  tag check still takes links and junctions out first, and each folder is checked again once it
  has been read: a folder swapped for a link in between is dropped, in the walk and in counting.
  Reads stay refused outside the KI either way (resolve + containment).
- Counting never starts after the budget ("not counted"); the tool handlers look at the clock after
  resolving the path, before is_file / is_dir.
- A missing-folder answer says "not looked at" when the scan was skipped; unchecked hidden entries
  are marked "(not checked)".
- Tests: a folder swapped for a link after the check (walk and count), the İ prefix, the handlers
  after a slow resolve.
